@page "/"

<PageTitle>RogueDeck Studio</PageTitle>

<div class="landing">
    <section class="landing-hero">
        <p class="hero-kicker">A Moonvine Forge tool</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title">
            Forge a whole roguelike.
            <span>No code. One document.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="hero-intro">
            Cards, enemies, relics, statuses, events, shops and a branching map — author every piece of a
            deckbuilding roguelike visually, playtest it on the spot, and take the result with you as a single
            JSON file.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
            <SampleQuickStart />
            <a class="hero-secondary" href="help">Read the guide</a>
        </div>
        <p class="hero-note muted">
            No account, no setup. Balanced ideas welcome. Broken ideas encouraged.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="landing-steps" aria-label="How it works">
        <article class="step-card">
            <p class="step-kicker">1 · Author</p>
            <h2>Every tab, one document</h2>
            <p>
                The <a href="hero">Hero</a>, the <a href="cards">Cards</a> &amp; deck, the
                <a href="encounters">Encounters</a>, <a href="relics">Relics</a>, <a href="events">Events</a> and
                <a href="shops">Shops</a> — each tab is a lens over the same run document, so everything you build
                connects.
            </p>
        </article>
        <article class="step-card">
            <p class="step-kicker">2 · Playtest</p>
            <h2>Play it immediately</h2>
            <p>
                <a href="playtest">Fight a single encounter</a> straight from the document, or assemble the map and
                drive the whole run seed by seed in the <a href="run">Run</a> tab — fights play out card by card.
            </p>
        </article>
        <article class="step-card">
            <p class="step-kicker">3 · Take it with you</p>
            <h2>Download your creation</h2>
            <p>
                The finished project is one JSON blueprint. Download it from the <a href="run">Run</a> tab, share
                it, and upload it later to keep working — it is the same contract the
                <a href="https://github.com/Paranoidgrinch/RogueDeck-Core" rel="noopener noreferrer"
                   target="_blank">RogueDeck Core engine</a> consumes.
            </p>
        </article>
    </section>

    <footer class="landing-foot">
        <span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <p>
            RogueDeck Studio is the authoring workbench for <strong>RogueDeck Core</strong>, a deterministic C#
            engine for roguelike deckbuilders — forged by
            <a href="https://moonvineforge.com" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Moonvine Forge</a>.
        </p>
        <a href="https://github.com/Paranoidgrinch/RogueDeck-Core" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
            Follow development →
        </a>
    </footer>
</div>
